Z||000000||-=shame=-||08-02-2000||06:19 PM||||OK. I purchased my first fiero about two months ago. I've done simple little fix-it-up crap. pads, a caliper, front shocks, tranny filter (auto V-6 GT '86) BUT. Now I don't know what I should focus my attention on first. I would welcome some suggestions but keep in mind that I like to keep things a little factory as opposed to droping in a V-8 or a holley carb. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||08-02-2000||06:39 PM||||shame first make plans to have the car shipped to me;  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>no.. ok, shame "Do What Ya Like"<BR>can you post some pics of your car???<BR>and how deep are your pockets?<BR>there are a lot of little mods that can<BR>be done to these little cars, most of then have been talked about and posted here.\<BR>A lot of the members have stock parts<BR>for sale in the mall, also take a look <BR>in the photo gallery!!!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723593&p=24416340&Sequence=2"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||08-02-2000||07:39 PM||||First thing I would do is get it running top notch. Then maybe work on the eye factor or "curb appeal" of the car. This makes it easier to keep throwing money at it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The first thing I did to my Fiero was add GT wheels and a spoiler. Then I added a V6 in place of the 4 banger. Wasn't happy with the notchback so I swapped in a fastback clip then did some interior work and added some hood vents. There are tons of things to do to your Fiero... make a list and check them off as you go. I'm on #10 out of 1,185 on my list  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Chris <BR>88 Fiero Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||08-02-2000||07:45 PM||||I always give my Fieros a tune-up of sorts when I first buy them.<BR>Plugs, wires, I pull the dist. and clean it and replace the pick up coil and ignition control module, rotor, and cap.<BR>I change all fluids and filters as well.<BR>Thats just what I do, but it helps tremendously. Gives the car a good hot spark, and fluid/filter changes are obvious.<BR>I then take it to one of those do it yourself carwashes and power clean the engine. <BR>These are things I do first, before any cosmetic changes..once it comes time for the looks, skys the limit man!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 08-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||-=shame=-||08-04-2000||08:17 AM||||Alright, so next thing on the list will be the plugs and wires like 7 suggested. The guy I bought it from said they had been done (but people don't lie do they?) But, she runs hot when in traffic, so I'll flush the radiator. The one thing that is really getting to me is this. The dipstick has carmalized crap on the end of it. Just have to drop the pan and see how bad it is. With that is there anything specific I should be careful of, or use a detergent before draining it?||||reg||5
Z||000005||chris west||08-04-2000||08:53 PM||||Will here bfrom West Coast Fiero to help you get some more ideas maybe you should check out our web site at <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A>  to help out get too many ideas to thing about doing to your car. Also the plugs wires modual and a coil would b a good idea.||||reg||1
